(732,23,49,'Sorting algorithms intro','**Selection sort** finds the smallest item and moves it to the front, then repeats for the rest.\n\nExample 1:\n```\nvar v = new List<int> { 5, 2, 9, 1 };\nint n = v.Count;\nfor (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {\n    int small = i;\n    for (int j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {\n        if (v[j] < v[small]) {\n            small = j;\n        }\n    }\n    int t = v[i];\n    v[i] = v[small];\n    v[small] = t;\n}\nforeach (int x in v) {\n    Console.WriteLine(x);\n}\n```\nOutput:\n```\n1\n2\n5\n9\n```\n\nExample 2:\n```\nvar v = new List<int> { 30, 10, 20 };\nint n = v.Count;\nfor (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {\n    int small = i;\n    for (int j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {\n        if (v[j] < v[small]) {\n            small = j;\n        }\n    }\n    int t = v[i];\n    v[i] = v[small];\n    v[small] = t;\n}\nConsole.WriteLine("" + (v[0]) + (" ") + (v[1]) + (" ") + (v[2]));\n```\nOutput:\n```\n10 20 30\n```\n\nExample 3:\n```\nvar v = new List<int> { 9, 2, 4, 1 };\nint n = v.Count;\nfor (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {\n    int small = i;\n    for (int j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {\n        if (v[j] < v[small]) {\n            small = j;\n        }\n    }\n    int t = v[i];\n    v[i] = v[small];\n    v[small] = t;\n}\nforeach (int x in v) {\n    Console.WriteLine(x);\n}\n```\nOutput:\n```\n1\n2\n4\n9\n```\n\nPractice: change the numbers or words in Example 1, then guess the new output before you run it.'),
(733,23,50,'Mini project','A small **grade book**: add up the scores, find the average and count how many students **passed**.\n\nExample 1:\n```\nvar scores = new List<int> { 70, 85, 90, 65 };\nint sum = 0;\nint pass = 0;\nforeach (int s in scores) {\n    sum += s;\n    if (s >= 70) {\n        pass++;\n    }\n}\nConsole.WriteLine("" + ("Average: ") + ((sum / scores.Count)));\nConsole.WriteLine("" + ("Passed: ") + (pass));\n```\nOutput:\n```\nAverage: 77\nPassed: 3\n```\n\nExample 2:\n```\nvar v = new List<int> { 4, 9, 6 };\nint big = v[0];\nint total = 0;\nforeach (int x in v) {\n    total += x;\n    if (x > big) {\n        big = x;\n    }\n}\nConsole.WriteLine("" + ("Total: ") + (total));\nConsole.WriteLine("" + ("Largest: ") + (big));\n```\nOutput:\n```\nTotal: 19\nLargest: 9\n```\n\nExample 3:\n```\nvar scores = new List<int> { 6, 4, 8, 9 };\nint sum = 0;\nint pass = 0;\nforeach (int s in scores) {\n    sum += s;\n    if (s >= 6) {\n        pass++;\n    }\n}\nConsole.WriteLine("" + ("Average: ") + ((sum / scores.Count)));\nConsole.WriteLine("" + ("Passed: ") + (pass));\n```\nOutput:\n```\nAverage: 6\nPassed: 3\n```\n\nPractice: change the numbers or words in Example 1, then guess the new output before you run it.'),
